    <span class="accordion-text">
      <span class="accordion-title">Customer Retention &amp; Risk</span>
      <span class="accordion-subtitle">Satisfaction drivers, dissatisfaction signals, switch risk, and retention plays</span>
    </span>
    <span class="accordion-icon">+</span>
  </summary>
  <div class="accordion-body">

    <h2>Satisfaction Drivers for BambooHR Customers</h2>
    <p>What BambooHR's current customers say the platform does well.<br/><span class="q-cite">Q16: {questionText.Q16}</span></p>
    <p class="avg-legend"><span class="avg-legend-line"></span> Dashed line = overall average (all 180 participants) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <span class="sig-mark">*</span> = statistically significant difference (p &lt; 0.05)</p>
    <div class="bar-chart">
      {d.q16_bamboo.filter((c: any) => c.pct >= 5).map((c: any) => (
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">{formatLabel(c.label)}</span>
          <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill teal" style={`width:${c.pct}%`}><span class="bar-val">{c.pct}%{c.sig && <span class="sig-mark">*</span>}</span></div>{c.all_pct != null && <div class="bar-avg" style={`left:${c.all_pct}%`}></div>}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">Source: Q16. BambooHR users only (n=60). Showing 5%+.</p>

    <h2>Dissatisfaction Signals</h2>
    <p>The frustrations and shortcomings that erode satisfaction among BambooHR's base.</p>

    <h3>Current Frustrations<span class="q-cite">Q17: {questionText.Q17}</span></h3>
    <p class="avg-legend"><span class="avg-legend-line"></span> Dashed line = overall average (all 180 participants) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <span class="sig-mark">*</span> = statistically significant difference (p &lt; 0.05)</p>
    <div class="bar-chart">
      {d.q17_bamboo.map((c: any) => (
        <div class="bar-row">
          <span class="bar-label">{formatLabel(c.label)}</span>
          <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill warm" style={`width:${c.pct}%`}><span class="bar-val">{c.pct}%{c.sig && <span class="sig-mark">*</span>}</span></div>{c.all_pct != null && <div class="bar-avg" style={`left:${c.all_pct}%`}></div>}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">Source: Q17. BambooHR users only (n=60).</p>

    <div class="vuln-callout">
      <p><strong>BambooHR's shortcomings cluster around integration and reporting.</strong> Payroll/HRIS integration friction stands out: 67% of BambooHR users cite it as a shortcoming, significantly above the overall average (p &lt; 0.05). Reporting inadequacy (62%) and poor system integration (50%) round out the top three.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Switch Risk Profile</h2>

    <h3>Likelihood to Re-Evaluate Within 6 Months<span class="q-cite">Q23: {questionText.Q23}</span></h3>
    <div class="crosstab">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="text-align:left">Likelihood</th>
            <th>BambooHR</th>
            <th>Gusto</th>
            <th>Rippling</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.q23_comparison_pw.map((row: any) => {
            const v1 = row.bamboo_pct;
            const v2 = row.gusto_pct;
            const v3 = row.rippling_pct;
            const maxV = Math.max(v1, v2, v3);
            return (
              <tr>
                <td style="text-align:left">{row.label}</td>
                <td class={v1 === maxV && v1 > 0 ? 'highlight' : ''} style="text-align:center">{v1}%{row.bamboo_sig && <span class="pw-sig">{row.bamboo_sig}</span>}</td>
                <td class={v2 === maxV && v2 > 0 ? 'highlight' : ''} style="text-align:center">{v2}%{row.gusto_sig && <span class="pw-sig">{row.gusto_sig}</span>}</td>
                <td class={v3 === maxV && v3 > 0 ? 'highlight' : ''} style="text-align:center">{v3}%{row.rippling_sig && <span class="pw-sig">{row.rippling_sig}</span>}</td>
              </tr>
            );
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">Source: Q23. {questionText.Q23} (n=60 per platform)</p>
    <p class="pw-legend">Superscript letters indicate the value is significantly higher (p &lt; 0.05) than: <strong>B</strong> = BambooHR, <strong>G</strong> = Gusto, <strong>R</strong> = Rippling</p>

    <div class="vuln-callout">
      <p><strong>BambooHR and Gusto users show significantly higher switching intent than Rippling users.</strong> 45% of both BambooHR and Gusto users say they are somewhat likely to re-evaluate within 6 months, compared to just 3% of Rippling users (p &lt; 0.05). Conversely, 42% of Rippling users say they are very unlikely to switch, significantly higher than BambooHR (5%) or Gusto (10%). When combined with the specific frustrations driving this intent (payroll friction, reporting gaps, integration pain), BambooHR has a clear picture of what to fix to prevent churn.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Retention Play Recommendations</h2>
    <table class="rec-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Risk Signal</th><th>CS Motion</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Payroll/HRIS integration friction (67%)</td><td>Proactive outreach to accounts using BambooHR + a separate payroll provider. Offer integration audit and configuration support. If native payroll is on the roadmap, share timeline with at-risk accounts early.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reporting inadequacy (62%)</td><td>Offer early access to any reporting improvements. Provide custom report templates. Assign a CS rep to help configure existing reporting features that may be underutilized.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Performance management gap (45%)</td><td>If performance management is on the roadmap, share beta access. If not, partner with a best-in-class performance tool and offer a bundled integration.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Switching intent (45% somewhat likely)</td><td>Implement a quarterly "health check" program for accounts showing engagement decline. Address frustrations before they become RFPs.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Value Perception: BambooHR vs. Competitors<span class="q-cite">Q21: {questionText.Q21}</span></h3>
    <div class="crosstab">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="text-align:left">Value Perception</th>
            <th>BambooHR</th>
            <th>Gusto</th>
            <th>Rippling</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.q21_comparison.bamboo.categories.map((cat: any) => {
            const gCat = d.q21_comparison.gusto.categories.find((c: any) => c.label === cat.label);
            const rCat = d.q21_comparison.rippling.categories.find((c: any) => c.label === cat.label);
            return (
              <tr>
                <td style="text-align:left">{cat.label}</td>
                <td style="text-align:center">{cat.pct}%</td>
                <td style="text-align:center">{gCat?.pct ?? 0}%</td>
                <td style="text-align:center">{rCat?.pct ?? 0}%</td>
              </tr>
            );
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">Source: Q21. {questionText.Q21} (n=60 per platform)</p>

  </div>
</details>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- SECTION 8: METHODOLOGY -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<details class="accordion">
  <summary class="accordion-header">
    <span class="accordion-num">08</span>
    <span class="accordion-text">
      <span class="accordion-title">Methodology</span>
      <span class="accordion-subtitle">Sample design, interview structure, coding process, and analytical approach</span>
    </span>
    <span class="accordion-icon">+</span>
  </summary>
  <div class="accordion-body">

    <h2>Sample Design</h2>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">180</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Participants</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">24</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Questions</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">153</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Thematic Codes</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">3</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Platforms (60 each)</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>The sample included 180 HR, People Operations, and Talent Acquisition leaders at companies with 50 to 1,000 employees. Participants were evenly distributed across three current platforms (BambooHR, Gusto, Rippling) and four company-size tiers to enable both platform-level and size-level comparisons.</p>

    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Company size tiers</td><td>50-100, 101-250, 251-500, 501-1,000 employees</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Industries</td><td>Technology, Healthcare, Professional Services, Financial Services, Retail, Education, Manufacturing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Seniority</td><td>Manager through C-suite, with concentration at Manager and Director levels</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Interview format</td><td>Semi-structured qualitative interviews, 24 questions covering the full purchase journey</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Coding Process</h2>
    <p>Interview transcripts were coded using a dual-coder AI-assisted methodology with human oversight. Two independent coding agents classified each response against a 153-code codebook developed through a multi-pass discovery process (extraction, clustering, validation, dimension architecture). An arbiter resolved disagreements. Inter-rater reliability was assessed using Cohen's weighted Kappa.</p>

    <h3>Inter-Rater Reliability</h3>
    <div class="stat-grid" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">0.935</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Overall Weighted Kappa</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">0.761</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Lowest Per-Code Kappa</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-num">82/82</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Codes Above 0.65 Threshold</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>The overall weighted Kappa of <strong>0.935</strong> falls in the "almost perfect" agreement range. By published standards, a Kappa above 0.80 is considered excellent for qualitative content analysis. A stricter threshold of 0.67 is sometimes applied in exploratory studies. Every individual code in this study exceeds that threshold, with the lowest per-code Kappa at 0.761 (Time Savings Enabling Strategic Work). The minimum acceptance threshold for this study was set at 0.65, and all 82 evaluated codes passed.</p>

    <div class="bamboo-callout">
      <p><strong>What this means for data quality:</strong> The high reliability scores indicate that the coding was applied consistently across all 180 transcripts. The data underlying every chart and cross-tab in this report reflects systematic, reproducible classification, not subjective interpretation. Findings built on these codes can be treated with confidence.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Analytical Approach for This Report</h2>
    <p>All statistics in this report are derived from the coded interview data (n=180). BambooHR-specific analyses filter to the 60 BambooHR users in the sample. Cross-platform comparisons use all 180 participants. Percentages represent the proportion of the relevant sample that was coded as positive for a given thematic code or category.</p>

    <p>This report was produced by BuyerVoice LLC using proprietary qualitative research methods and AI-assisted analytical tools.</p>

  </div>
</details>

</div> <!-- end container -->

<div class="footer-print">
  <p>BuyerVoice LLC &bull; BambooHR Strategic Review &bull; April 2026 &bull; Confidential</p>
</div>

<!-- Verbatim drill-down data -->
<Fragment set:html={vdScript} />
<script is:inline define:vars={{ bambooRejectorPids: d.bamboo_rejector_pids, bambooRejectorCodePids: d.bamboo_rejector_code_pids }}>
  window.__BAMBOO_REJECTOR_PIDS = bambooRejectorPids;
  window.__BAMBOO_REJECTOR_CODE_PIDS = bambooRejectorCodePids;
</script>

<!-- Verbatim modal -->
<div class="vb-overlay" id="vbOverlay">
  <div class="vb-dialog">
    <button class="vb-close" id="vbClose">&times;</button>
    <div class="vb-header">
      <h3 id="vbTitle"></h3>
      <p id="vbSubtitle"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="vb-body" id="vbBody"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline>
(function(){
  var VD = window.__VD;
  var VQ = window.__VQ;
  if (!VD || !VQ) return;

  function escHtml(s) {
    var d = document.createElement('div');
    d.appendChild(document.createTextNode(s));
    return d.innerHTML;
  }

  function annotateCharts() {
    var sourceNotes = document.querySelectorAll('.source-note');
    sourceNotes.forEach(function(note) {
      var m = note.textContent.match(/Source:\s*Q(\d+)\./);
      if (!m) return;
      var qid = 'Q' + m[1];

      var thematicQs = ['Q4','Q7','Q8','Q9','Q11','Q12','Q14','Q15','Q16','Q17','Q18','Q19','Q24'];
      var catQs = ['Q1','Q10','Q13','Q21'];

      var isThematic = thematicQs.indexOf(qid) !== -1;
      var isCat = catQs.indexOf(qid) !== -1;
      if (!isThematic && !isCat) return;

      var barChart = note.previousElementSibling;
      while (barChart && !barChart.classList.contains('bar-chart')) {
        barChart = barChart.previousElementSibling;
      }
      if (!barChart) return;

      // Skip if this bar chart was already annotated by a closer source note
      if (barChart.getAttribute('data-annotated')) return;
      barChart.setAttribute('data-annotated', 'true');

      // Detect tool filter from source note text (e.g., "BambooHR users only")
      var toolFilter = '';
      var pidFilter = '';
      var noteText = note.textContent || '';
      if (noteText.indexOf('considered but rejected') !== -1) pidFilter = 'bamboo_rejectors';
      else if (noteText.indexOf('BambooHR users only') !== -1) toolFilter = 'BambooHR';
      else if (noteText.indexOf('Gusto users only') !== -1) toolFilter = 'Gusto';
      else if (noteText.indexOf('Rippling users only') !== -1) toolFilter = 'Rippling';

      var rows = barChart.querySelectorAll('.bar-row');
      rows.forEach(function(row) {
        var labelEl = row.querySelector('.bar-label');
        if (!labelEl) return;
        var label = labelEl.textContent.trim();
        row.setAttribute('data-drilldown', 'true');
        row.setAttribute('data-q', qid);
        row.setAttribute('data-code', label);
        row.setAttribute('data-type', isThematic ? 'code' : 'cat');
        if (toolFilter) row.setAttribute('data-tool', toolFilter);
        if (pidFilter) row.setAttribute('data-pid-filter', pidFilter);
      });
    });
  }

  annotateCharts();

  var overlay = document.getElementById('vbOverlay');
  var titleEl = document.getElementById('vbTitle');
  var subtitleEl = document.getElementById('vbSubtitle');
  var bodyEl = document.getElementById('vbBody');
  var closeBtn = document.getElementById('vbClose');

  var BAMBOO_REJECTOR_PIDS = window.__BAMBOO_REJECTOR_PIDS || [];
  var BAMBOO_REJECTOR_CODE_PIDS = window.__BAMBOO_REJECTOR_CODE_PIDS || {};

  function normCode(s) {
    return s.toLowerCase().replace(/-/g, ' ').replace(/_/g, ' ');
  }

  function openModal(qid, codeName, matchType, toolFilter, pidFilterName) {
    var normName = normCode(codeName);
    var allowedPids = null;
    if (pidFilterName === 'bamboo_rejectors') {
      // Use per-code PID list: only participants who rejected BambooHR for THIS specific reason
      allowedPids = BAMBOO_REJECTOR_CODE_PIDS[normName] || BAMBOO_REJECTOR_PIDS;
    }
    var matches = [];
    VD.forEach(function(p) {
      // Apply PID filter if specified (e.g., BambooHR rejectors only)
      if (allowedPids && allowedPids.indexOf(p.pid) === -1) return;
      // Apply tool filter if specified
      if (toolFilter && p.tool !== toolFilter) return;

      // When using per-code PID filter (e.g., BambooHR rejectors), the PID list
      // already identifies exactly who to show. Skip code matching because the
      // verbatim data has general Q15 codes while the CSV has vendor-specific ones.
      if (allowedPids) {
        if (p.v[qid]) matches.push(p);
        return;
      }

      var hit = false;
      if (matchType === 'code') {
        var codes = p.c[qid];
        if (codes) {
          for (var i = 0; i < codes.length; i++) {
            if (normCode(codes[i]) === normName) {
              hit = true;
              break;
            }
          }
        }
      } else {
        var cat = p.cat[qid];
        if (cat) {
          if (Array.isArray(cat)) {
            for (var j = 0; j < cat.length; j++) {
              if (normCode(cat[j]) === normName) {
                hit = true;
                break;
              }
            }
          } else if (normCode(cat) === normName) {
            hit = true;
          }
        }
      }
      if (hit && p.v[qid]) {
        matches.push(p);
      }
    });

    var filterLabel = pidFilterName === 'bamboo_rejectors' ? ' — participants who rejected BambooHR' : (toolFilter ? ' — ' + toolFilter + ' users only' : '');
    titleEl.textContent = codeName + ' (' + matches.length + ' participant' + (matches.length !== 1 ? 's' : '') + ')' + filterLabel;
    subtitleEl.textContent = VQ[qid] || '';

    bodyEl.innerHTML = '';
    if (matches.length === 0) {
      bodyEl.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#6B6B6B;font-size:13px;">No matching verbatims found.</p>';
    } else {
      matches.forEach(function(p) {
        var card = document.createElement('div');
        card.className = 'vb-card';

        var fullText = p.v[qid];
        var truncated = fullText.length > 500;
        var shortText = truncated ? fullText.substring(0, 500) + '...' : fullText;

        var quoteDiv = document.createElement('div');
        quoteDiv.className = 'vb-quote';
        quoteDiv.textContent = shortText;
        card.appendChild(quoteDiv);

        if (truncated) {
          var moreBtn = document.createElement('button');
          moreBtn.className = 'vb-more';
          moreBtn.textContent = 'Show more';
          var expanded = false;
          moreBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
            expanded = !expanded;
            quoteDiv.textContent = expanded ? fullText : shortText;
            moreBtn.textContent = expanded ? 'Show less' : 'Show more';
          });
          card.appendChild(moreBtn);
        }

        var tagsDiv = document.createElement('div');
        tagsDiv.className = 'vb-tags';
        var tags = [p.sen, p.sz, p.ind, p.tool].filter(Boolean);
        tags.forEach(function(t) {
          var span = document.createElement('span');
          span.className = 'vb-tag';
          span.textContent = t;
          tagsDiv.appendChild(span);
        });
        card.appendChild(tagsDiv);

        bodyEl.appendChild(card);
      });
    }

    overlay.classList.add('open');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }

  function closeModal() {
    overlay.classList.remove('open');
    document.body.style.overflow = '';
  }

  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
  overlay.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
    if (e.target === overlay) closeModal();
  });
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && overlay.classList.contains('open')) closeModal();
  });

  document.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
    var row = e.target.closest('[data-drilldown]');
    if (!row) return;
    var qid = row.getAttribute('data-q');
    var code = row.getAttribute('data-code');
    var type = row.getAttribute('data-type') || 'code';
    var tool = row.getAttribute('data-tool') || '';
    var pidFilterName = row.getAttribute('data-pid-filter') || '';
    openModal(qid, code, type, tool, pidFilterName);
  });
})();
</script>

</body>
</html>
